research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cex-composition-of-limits-fails.md-196-[L2] Every real is a limit point of $\mathbb{R}$, punctured neighbourhoods being never empty ([[def-limit-point-r]], [[def-neighbourhood-r]]).
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cex-composition-of-limits-fails.md-197-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cex-composition-of-limits-fails.md-198-[L3] The witness function: $f(0) = 1$ by its definition, and the limit of $f$ at $0$ exists and equals $0$, as verified in [[cex-limit-differs-from-the-value]].
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cex-composition-of-limits-fails.md-199-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cex-composition-of-limits-fails.md-200-[L4] Absolute value: $|0| = 0$; $|u| = 0$ exactly when $u = 0$ ([[lem-of-abs-value]]).
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cex-composition-of-limits-fails.md-201-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cex-composition-of-limits-fails.md-202-[L5] Order in $\mathbb{R}$: trichotomy, and $0 < 1$, so $1 \ne 0$ ([[cor-of-one-positive]], [[def-ordered-field]]).
