research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cex-composition-of-limits-fails.md:204:[L6] Composition of limits, and its two extra hypotheses: (i) $L \in B$ and $f(L) = M$; (ii) some real $\eta > 0$ has $g(x) \ne L$ for every $x \in A$ with $0 < |x - c| < \eta$ ([[thm-composition-of-function-limits]]).
