research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json:13824:          "claim": "Both extra hypotheses of [[thm-composition-of-function-limits]] fail for the pair $(f, g)$: hypothesis (i) fails because $L = 0$ lies in $B = \\mathbb{R}$ while $f(L) = f(0) = 1 \\ne 0 = M$, and hypothesis (ii) fails because $g(x) = 0 = L$ for every $x$, so no punctured neighbourhood of $0$ avoids the value $L$. For the pair $(f, \\iota)$, hypothesis (ii) does hold with $\\eta := 1$, since $\\iota(x) = x \\ne 0$ whenever $0 < |x - 0| < 1$; and step 3.2 confirms the conclusion of the theorem there.",
