research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-13731-          "quote": "An **ordered field** is a field $F$ ([[def-field]]) together with a subset\n$P \\subseteq F$, the set of **positive** elements (the *positive cone*),\nsatisfying:\n\n- **(O1) Trichotomy.** For each $x \\in F$, exactly one of the following holds:\n  $x \\in P$, or $x = 0$, or $-x \\in P$.\n- **(O2) Closure.** If $x, y \\in P$ then $x + y \\in P$ and $x \\cdot y \\in P$.\n\nWe write $x > 0$ for $x \\in P$ (read \"$x$ is positive\"), and define the order by\n\n$$a < b \\;:\\Longleftrightarrow\\; b - a \\in P, \\qquad a \\le b \\;:\\Longleftrightarrow\\; a < b \\text{ or } a = b.$$\n\nThus $a > b$ means $b < a$, and $a \\ge b$ means $b \\le a$. An element $x$ with\n$-x \\in P$ (equivalently $x < 0$) is called **negative**.",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-13732-          "uses": [
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-13733-            "1.3",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-13734-            "4.1"
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-13735-          ]
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-13736-        },
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-13737-        {
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-13738-          "fact": "L6",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json:13739:          "source": "thm-composition-of-function-limits",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-13740-          "source_section": "Statement",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-13741-          "quote": "Let $A, B \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}$, let $g : A \\to \\mathbb{R}$ with\n$g(A) \\subseteq B$, and let $f : B \\to \\mathbb{R}$, so that the composite\n$f \\circ g : A \\to \\mathbb{R}$ is defined. Let $c$ be a limit point of $A$ and\n$L$ a limit point of $B$ ([[def-limit-point-r]]), and suppose the limits\n\n$$\\lim_{x \\to c} g(x) = L \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad \\lim_{y \\to L} f(y) = M$$\n\nboth exist, with the stated values ([[def-function-limit]]). Suppose in addition\nthat **at least one** of the following holds:\n\n- **(i)** $L \\in B$ and $f(L) = M$;\n- **(ii)** there is a real $\\eta > 0$ with $g(x) \\ne L$ for every $x \\in A$\n  satisfying $0 < |x - c| < \\eta$.\n\nThen the limit of $f \\circ g$ at $c$ **exists**, and\n\n$$\\lim_{x \\to c} f\\bigl(g(x)\\bigr) \\;=\\; \\lim_{y \\to L} f(y) \\;=\\; M .$$\n\n**At least one extra hypothesis is necessary.** With both omitted the statement is\nfalse, and [[fs-naive-composition-of-limits]] refutes it with a two-line witness\nin which (i) fails because $f(L) \\ne M$ and (ii) fails because $g$ is constantly\nequal to $L$.\n\n**Why an extra hypothesis is needed at all.** The inner limit controls $g(x)$\nonly up to $|g(x) - L| < \\rho$; it does not prevent $g(x)$ from *equalling* $L$.\nBut [[def-function-limit]] says nothing about $f$ at the point $L$, so the outer\nestimate is unavailable exactly at the values $g(x) = L$. Hypothesis (i) supplies\nthe missing value directly; hypothesis (ii) excludes those values.",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-13742-          "uses": [
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-13743-            "4.2"
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-13744-          ]
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-13745-        }
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.proof-contracts.json-13746-      ],
