research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-naive-composition-of-limits.prompt.md-1067-**Given:** The set $A := \mathbb{R}$, the point $c := 0$, and the function $f : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ defined by $f(x) := 0$ for $x \ne 0$ and $f(0) := 1$.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-naive-composition-of-limits.prompt.md-1068-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-naive-composition-of-limits.prompt.md-1069-[L1] The limit condition: $\lim_{x \to c} h(x) = L$ means that for every real $\varepsilon > 0$ there is a real $\delta > 0$ such that every $x$ in the domain of $h$ with $0 < |x - c| < \delta$ satisfies $|h(x) - L| < \varepsilon$ ([[def-function-limit]]).
