research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-composition-of-limits-fails.prompt.md-1320-2.1 By trichotomy [L2] each $x$ lies in exactly one of the cases 1.1-1.3, and in each we verified $|x| \ge 0$, that $|x| = 0 \iff x = 0$, that $|-x| = |x|$, and that $-|x| \le x \le |x|$; hence all four hold for every $x$. [step 1.1, step 1.2, step 1.3, cases-exhaustive]
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-composition-of-limits-fails.prompt.md-1321-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-composition-of-limits-fails.prompt.md-1322-2.2 By trichotomy [L2] each pair $x, y$ lies in exactly one of the cases 1.4-1.6, and in each $|xy| = |x|\,|y|$; hence $|xy| = |x|\,|y|$ for all $x, y$. [step 1.4, step 1.5, step 1.6, cases-exhaustive]
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-composition-of-limits-fails.prompt.md-1323-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-composition-of-limits-fails.prompt.md-1324-3.1 Let $c > 0$: if $|x| < c$ then $-c < -|x| \le x \le |x| < c$ by [step 2.1] and [L2], so $-c < x < c$; conversely if $-c < x < c$ then both $x < c$ and $-x < c$, and since $|x|$ equals $x$ or $-x$ by [L1], we get $|x| < c$, so $|x| < c \iff -c < x < c$. [step 2.1, L1, L2] ∎
